{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566508-the-three-heads-of-kerberos-clarification","id":566508,"title":"The Three Heads of Kerberos Clarification","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-24T09:07:52-07:00","id":566508,"title":"The Three Heads of Kerberos Clarification","content":"Hello , this is actually my very first post here. I have recently started playing a Kerebos in my local game.<br /> <br /> My question broadly involves &quot;Lashing Out&quot;, I know this is suppose to be a social taboo or something amongst Kindred. The Kerebos , as the masters of lashing out, get all sorts of advantages with The Three Heads of Kerberos merits but must constantly be breaking this social norm just to not suffer their bloodline bane.<br /> <br /> So my broad question is &quot; Is there a subtle way to apply Predator's Aura to someone?&quot;<br /> <br /> Secondly I am confused by the fourth level of the merit, the way it is written:<br /> <br /> <b>Striking (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Your character infects with her Beast through other actions beyond lashing out. By spending a Willpower point, she can lash out reflexively, so long as she\u2019s affecting the victim with something else simultaneously. Most commonly, this means slashing a victim with her claws while infecting them with the Beast. But it could mean using it while investigating them with Auspex, shooting them with a pistol, while entrancing them with Majesty, while feeding them her blood, while seductively touching them, feeding from them, or any other number of effects.<br /> <br /> Make seems that it is allowing you to lash out in addition to attacking/ using a discipline. But it also mentions &quot;seductively touching&quot; someone. Can not all Kindred do this, touching someone , in a non combative way, does not take an action does it? If so this makes sense but if not why bring it up? That combined with the wording at the beginning &quot;Your character infects with her Beast through other actions beyond lashing out.&quot; makes me feel as if THIS is a way to inflict your aura on someone subtlety. My ST says it is not, but I feel it is.<br /> <br /> Am I completely wrong? Anyone who could clarify these questions for me would be a huge help to me. Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6597-dragonmarkedson","name":"Dragonmarkedson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:03:39-07:00","id":566628,"title":"","content":"The action of Lashing Out is normally an instant action, which means you can't lash out and do something else in the same turn. With the merit you can lash out as a reflexive action in conjunction with another instant action.<br /> <br /> Seducing someone requires a persuasion roll (usually extended). Mechanically you and your seduction target take adversarial roles to determine success/failure. Same as shooting someone.<br /> <br /> There's nothing subtle about lashing out. The other person knows you did 'something' to them and in the case of it being another vampire they know you flashed your Beast at them in order to incite a specific reaction from their own Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:41:19-07:00","id":566673,"title":"","content":"I don't think there really is a subtle way. I mean, while its not exactly something mortals would pick up on, I think among Kindred its something obvious by the feel of the aura. If it was subtle, then it would kind of defeat the purpose of it being taboo - there would be lots of uses and no one would say a word, because how would they know? <br /> <br /> That's one of the advantages of Disciplines over Lashing Out - they're subtle and the people don't really know they're under your control. <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the fourth dot? Tsusasi covered the issue. Its main use is in combat, where the number of actions per turn matter. Social situations? Not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T13:17:10-07:00","id":568290,"title":"","content":"Not to say that you cant use it in a social setting. Your character has majesty, kicks on awe in a night club and starts flinging the seductive beast at people. Soon you have a room full of mortals that just want to get down and .... -cough-<br /> <br /> Not saying this is a smart idea... it is just a non combative use of it. There are other many other scenarios too which you could use this out of combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T13:44:01-07:00","id":568325,"title":"","content":"You can use the fourth dot out of combat... but it rarely matters. Combat is the only time we really keep track of things in the matter of turns, so outside of combat? It doesn't matter if you use the Predator's Aura at the same time as you activate Majesty, or you activate the Aura and Majesty a few seconds later. <br /> <br /> There might be some situation where the timing matters outside of a fight, but not that I'm really aware of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T14:32:47-07:00","id":568389,"title":"","content":"I don't think it is a social taboo, is it?<br /> <br /> It seems an effective and pragmatic way of putting others in their places without necessarily resorting to violence. It's probably gauche to do it in certain situations, like in one of the subtle Elysium or in the middle of a Prince's speech, but I don't see where it's considered taboo at all. The books were full of instances where Lashing Out would have been a much more acceptable option to what the vampires did.<br /> <br /> As for subtle, it's not necessarily something anyone beyond the one Lashing Out and their target would have to recognize, especially with the seductive or competitive beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-25-2015, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T14:56:54-07:00","id":568409,"title":"","content":"Yeah, think about what Lashing Out would look like from an outside observer's perspective. A Nosferatu gives someone a nasty look and they get all on-edge. A Daeva flirts with someone and they get a little extra frisky. A Ventrue talks down to someone and they get indignant and want to prove their superiority. Any of these could easily be the results of Lashing Out, the effects of a Discipline, or a completely mundane interaction. How would anyone but the victim know the difference?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T15:25:42-07:00","id":568428,"title":"","content":"I think the taboo was for triggering frenzy not the other possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T15:39:07-07:00","id":568446,"title":"","content":"I was illustrating why it's subtle. I imagine it would be taboo, but it's also pretty hard to police. When someone Frenzies and tries to blame it on someone else Lashing Out at them... What can you do? All you have is their word, there's no way to prove they didn't just Frenzy because they were hungry, or even intentionally Rode the Wave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T16:34:58-07:00","id":568496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566508-the-three-heads-of-kerberos-clarification?p=568428#post568428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the taboo was for triggering frenzy not the other possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lashing out doesn't trigger frenzy, though. Not inherently. The Monstrous Beast can give a penalty to resist frenzying.<br /> <br /> But otherwise while it can, that's more the frenzied one's fault, as they should have kept control. Don't accept a challenge you can't stand to lose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T18:24:19-07:00","id":568569,"title":"","content":"In character it is the same as a frenzy. One vampire lashes out at another forcing the other to fight back or run away. There may not be any mechanical bonuses for a frenzy, but appearances matter too. Since vampires can sense the predator aura unless it is suppressed, I would imagine they can sense someone lashing out if they are observing it happen. I don't know that it actually says it is taboo, but I can't see how vampires would consider it acceptable to go around lashing out to other vampires when witnesses are around. The purpose is to put someone in their place. That isn't exactly a class act. Taboo is too strong a word for how it is viewed. Observers would likely look down on all involved. One is weak for needed to use such force, the other for succumbing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T22:12:30-07:00","id":568798,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure it was stated that they can't sense when people lash out, unless they're being lashed out against or initiating it. I'll dig for the thread where it was said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T04:48:21-07:00","id":569030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566508-the-three-heads-of-kerberos-clarification?p=568569#post568569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In character it is the same as a frenzy. One vampire lashes out at another forcing the other to fight back or run away. There may not be any mechanical bonuses for a frenzy, but appearances matter too. Since vampires can sense the predator aura unless it is suppressed, I would imagine they can sense someone lashing out if they are observing it happen. I don't know that it actually says it is taboo, but I can't see how vampires would consider it acceptable to go around lashing out to other vampires when witnesses are around. The purpose is to put someone in their place. That isn't exactly a class act. Taboo is too strong a word for how it is viewed. Observers would likely look down on all involved. One is weak for needed to use such force, the other for succumbing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But the 'fighting back' of Lashing Out isn't actual fighting, it's just another posture, a snarl, a growl, a come-hither look or snarky comment about chess playing ability. Frenzy is a full on, violent give into the Beast. The Predatory Aura section even notes this, it's <i>implied </i>violence, not actual violence.<br /> <br /> And no, the section doesn't say anything about it being taboo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-26-2015, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T06:55:33-07:00","id":569159,"title":"","content":"The difference is that other vampires can feel the Auras. They feel every action of other vampires laden with that aura. When you're lashing out, your every actions intensify the aura. Can fellow Kindred really not feel an aura that's being sharpened to the point you're &quot;forcing fight or flight instincts?&quot; That's a direct quote.<br /> <br /> Remember, these aren't coy, sly words. We're using the full blunt force of your Presence and other Power Attributes; there's no Finesse involved. We're not talking about hints of power, or subtle maneuvering. Its forceful. Another vampire watching should see the challenge inherent in the actions if its enough to provoke a flight/fight response, before we even touch on their sensitivity to the aura in the first place.<br /> <br /> Nothing about the Lashing Out section suggests acting subtly at all. I don't think that the words they use here evoke that image at all. Seriously, the phrase &quot;lashing out&quot; alone suggests violence or extravagant actions. The constant references to fight or flight. Growling and threats, telling gazes, and drawing lines in the sand are not subtle actions. Its all about immediate actions, the vampy equivalent to surges of adrenaline.<br /> <br /> Sorry, Charlaquin, but I don't think your descriptions of &quot;how it can be subtle&quot; really works; its nothing at all of what I pick up from the section in question. Sure, if no one is paying attention, then no one will notice it. The Predator's Aura relies on being able to see, hear, or touch the other vampire. And mortals would likely be clueless. But those of the Blood watching the exchange? Between the obvious cues and feeling the aura? I can't see how it wouldn't be obvious to anyone with the least amount of empathy from the basic social cues.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for how its taboo? Well, I think that's more of an issue of Elysium than anything. Picking fights in Elysium is generally frowned on, and, in a very real sense, that's exactly what Lashing Out is. Elysium is the place where Kindred are supposed to play the game, be nice, and smile at each other without barring fangs, where rudeness and boorish behavior have potentially fatal consequences. Outside of Elysium, though? Or the local Elysium customs allows it? All bets are off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-26-2015, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T07:50:00-07:00","id":569200,"title":"","content":"I think the Predatory Aura suffers slightly from the text using two different interpretations. I can only assume it's a relic of 1e. It's stated that the perception is based on smell, touch, sight, and that it can be one-sided where one vampire perceives the other and not vice-versa. But then we also get talk about it being an aura that precludes civility between vampire, painting Kindred as wild animals barely reigned in by the rules and codes and Traditions they live by.<br /> <br /> I mean, reading the section a few times over, it barely even seems supernatural at all. Only the fact that the conditions seem disproportional to the mundane actions performed gives any indication it's magic.<br /> <br /> I mean, you shoot a flirty wink across the bar, and the target gets to either get flustered and bails or become more pliable to further flirting. It's a subtle power. The effects are well within the realm of mundane possibility. They only nudge the target, they don't force anything.<br /> <br /> Aside from about two lines that seem to reference to 1e's &quot;frenzy on sight&quot; mechanic, it really seems like the Predatory Aura refers to how vampires move differently, smell differently, and look differently, rather than anything supernatural.<br /> <br /> This leads to some confusion as to how one can intensify &quot;breathing unnaturally shallow and smelling like mortal blood&quot; into &quot;make everyone want to sleep with me with a glance.&quot;<br /> <br /> I suspect this is the root of the confusion between people who think it's subtle and people who think it can't be. The text seems a bit conflicted.<br /> <br /> Of course, it also talks a lot about Lashing Out being the Beast itself. The text also seems a bit conflicted as to whether or not the Beast is a literal entity sharing a Vampire's head or a metaphor for the unique needs and desires that a bloodsucking parasite has.<br /> <br /> Personally, I run it as both subtle and subtext. If you Lash Out and they turn it back on you, there's nothing more to say. They've established dominance. If you Lash Out and succeed, there's nothing more to say. You've established dominance. Vampires just don't talk about it, even when it happens. It doesn't really even have an IC name in the book (who's going to go &quot;you lashed out at me!&quot;?).<br /> <br /> The sheer fact that you can lose and have it turned on you is enough punishment without really needing to make it taboo, in my mind. Might makes right in Vampire-land, and might doesn't just mean strength of arms. If you win, you win. If you lose, you lose. Both cases may or may not end up in allies getting called against you if you wronged someone in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T08:03:05-07:00","id":569208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566508-the-three-heads-of-kerberos-clarification?p=569200#post569200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sheer fact that you can lose and have it turned on you is enough punishment without really needing to make it taboo, in my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div> Unless you ruin someone else's party with your actions. Then that's an even worse faux pas. Actually, I like faux pas for the Lashing Out more than taboo. Elysium bars violence, and that's the only situation I can think of where such violence is not a part of vampire life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T08:05:46-07:00","id":569212,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to leave these here...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/167874-lashing-out-and-awe?p=169331#post169331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also keep in mind that nobody besides the participants perceive the effects of lashing out... they only see the physical actions the vampires take to lash out and resist. So when the Gangrel resists the Daeva's Awe, people see her growl menacingly or sidle up with a distracting and sharp-toothed smile, and they see the Daeva's response. They don't perceive the supernatural contest that underlies that interaction.<br /> <br /> The predatory aura is called an &quot;aura&quot; because it's an ambient effect that allows vampires to recognize each other. Lashing out is focusing the aura on one person and cracking it like a whip.<br /> <br /> Other vampire capabilities are actually manifestations of the aura. For example, Awe itself is &quot;tinting&quot; your aura to show you in a good light, while Face in the Crowd is turning your predatory aura inwards so that neither peer nor prey notices you.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/167874-lashing-out-and-awe?p=169366#post169366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yeah, aura cues come in via a vampire's normal senses. You feel a pulseless body press against you in a crowd, or you see the light glinting off of a rival predator's teeth. But mechanically, it's passive and ambient.<br /> <br /> This is actually true of Awe or Dread Presence or whatever as well. A vampire using Awe moves and acts more appealingly than her plain jane date. Vampires deal with almost everything in material, perceptible terms, even when we as players adjudicate it in terms of abstract effects.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/167874-lashing-out-and-awe?p=169371#post169371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you just run it as psychic, nothing breaks. Certainly, a lot of times when you're hurrying through a section of the game, you might just name the game mechanic and move on. But the idea is that the predatory aura and the social Disciplines and things like that can be portrayed as things that happen in the world. Someone may seem just a little wrong, but if you focus, it's because they're leaning in too close, or because there's something a little menacing about the way their smile doesn't reach their eyes.<br /> <br /> Vampires can achieve things that don't seem possible through mundane means, but no one perceives the effects of supernatural powers in abstract terms. Think of it as showing the Disciplines without CGI.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T08:09:09-07:00","id":569216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566508-the-three-heads-of-kerberos-clarification?p=569200#post569200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I run it as both subtle and subtext. If you Lash Out and they turn it back on you, there's nothing more to say. They've established dominance. If you Lash Out and succeed, there's nothing more to say. You've established dominance. Vampires just don't talk about it, even when it happens. It doesn't really even have an IC name in the book (who's going to go &quot;you lashed out at me!&quot;?).<br /> <br /> The sheer fact that you can lose and have it turned on you is enough punishment without really needing to make it taboo, in my mind. Might makes right in Vampire-land, and might doesn't just mean strength of arms. If you win, you win. If you lose, you lose. Both cases may or may not end up in allies getting called against you if you wronged someone in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I run it much the same. It can be subtle or not. I think the lashing with the seductive beast is the most subtle to on lookers because all it requires is a whisper or a look. I also cant manage to find anything where it says it's &quot;taboo&quot; or where it causes &quot;frenzy&quot;. I asked once about the flavor text by the Triad box and Rose informed me that is how the victim is suppose to act once they have been &quot;Infected&quot; with the beast along with the condition's wording to make it appropriate. But none of those actually send you into a frenzy one just makes it harder to resist. <br /> <br /> As for knowing what happened to you... I wouldnt say it is an automatic knowledge that something happened because it doesnt say it there. you either get surly, hot, or aggressive, or turn your back on the whole thing making yourself look foolish or inferier in response to whatever was said or done. I would perhaps give another vampire or a ghoul an occult roll after the fact and deep consideration, but i dont see how a human would know that something otherworldly was done to them. Personally, I think it falls into line with Awe and Dread Presence. You dont really know something supernatural happened only that you feel different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T08:11:37-07:00","id":569219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566508-the-three-heads-of-kerberos-clarification?p=569200#post569200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you shoot a flirty wink across the bar, and the target gets to either get flustered and bails or become more pliable to further flirting. It's a subtle power. The effects are well within the realm of mundane possibility. They only nudge the target, they don't force anything.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's very much NOT the interpretation I get. A flirty wink is not lashing out in any way. Its not a way to initiate a flight or flight response.<br /> <br /> Lashing Out isn't just a name for what happens metaphysically. Its how your character <i>physically acts.</i> Even people without any hint of the magical effects would say you were verbally or physically lashing out at someone. <br /> <br /> You're drawing lines, you're growling, your giving heavy, meaningful stares. While these are mundane actions, they're not subtle mundane actions either.<br /> <br /> There's nothing in the wording that suggests subtlety. The attributes selected are not subtle. The effects are not subtle. The example actions are not subtle. I see nothing in the entire section that suggests subtlety. <br /> <br /> &quot;Further, a vampire can voluntarily intensify her predatory aura to elicit a reaction. Against other Kindred, this escalates the encounter, forcing fight or flight instincts.&quot; <br /> &quot;To lash out, the vampire must take a simple action appropriate to the aspect of predator used. A monstrous Beast growls, threatens, gnashes teeth, or calls to action. A seductive Beast sidles up to the prey, whispers beautiful lies, or gives a telling gaze from across the crowd. A competitive Beast draws a line in the sand, announces terms, or takes the role of mouse in a chase.&quot; <br /> <br /> At best, you can consider the Seductive Beast to be subtle, but absolutely not the others! And, even then?<br /> <br /> &quot;The Seductive Beast: This is the Beast-As-Tempter. It needs hot abandon, and a temporary escape from reality. It inspires the need for immediate, throwaway coupling. It evokes the primal need for instant gratification&quot; <br /> <br /> A coy wink from across the room does not evoke hot abandon and a need for immediate sexual gratification, not like a heavy, poignant stare. Not like sidling up to someone and whispering in their ear. The wink is not an appropriate action for evoking that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-26-2015, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T08:15:19-07:00","id":569221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566508-the-three-heads-of-kerberos-clarification?p=569219#post569219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's very much NOT the interpretation I get. A flirty wink is not lashing out in any way. Its not a way to initiate a flight or flight response.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is for the Seductive Beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lashing Out isn't just a name for what happens metaphysically. Its how your character <i>physically acts.</i> Even people without any hint of the magical effects would say you were verbally or physically lashing out at someone.<br /> <br /> You're drawing lines, you're growling, your giving heavy, meaningful stares. </div> </div> </div>That's just for the Monstrous Beast.<br /> <br /> Fight or flight is not literal when it comes to Lashing Out. Lashing out demands a response, either confront it and 'fight' or retreat or back off and 'flight.' It's not actually fighting or running away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-26-2015, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T08:48:03-07:00","id":569256,"title":"","content":"I think we're getting caught up here on different definitions of &quot;subtle.&quot; When I say subtle, I don't mean sneaky. Obviously bearing your teeth and snarling is an overt thing to do. What I mean is that it's difficult, if not impossible to distinguish whether the person doing it is Lashing Out, or actually just bearing their teeth and snarling, with no supernatural weight behind it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T08:55:47-07:00","id":569281,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Rose seems to have pre-emptively covered whether or not it's subtle anyways. <br /> <br /> I was just surprised to see someone thinking it was taboo, I figured I missed a book or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T09:16:21-07:00","id":569302,"title":"","content":"EDIT - you know, this thing is going nowhere, so I'm just going to say we agree to disagree. From my perspective, I see people telling me what's being written in the book is wrong, and I don't see myself as in the wrong, so that's my cue to just back off here. We all play different ways, and if that's how you have fun, not my place to correct you, just as I'll be having fun with my interpretation at my game. Lets all just have fun gaming. <br /> <br /> I'm just going to leave with this, though:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566508-the-three-heads-of-kerberos-clarification?p=569281#post569281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Rose seems to have pre-emptively covered whether or not it's subtle anyways.<br /> <br /> I was just surprised to see someone thinking it was taboo, I figured I missed a book or something.</div> </div> </div> </div> The taboo / social faux pas thing was covered by the writers too. That's where its coming from. That's where I got it, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-26-2015, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T09:24:12-07:00","id":569305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566508-the-three-heads-of-kerberos-clarification?p=569302#post569302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I didn't captialize &quot;lash out&quot; because Lashing Out includes the mudane definition of lashing out as well; you're physically and verbally lashing out. Seductive beast is trying to provoke an immediate need for pleasures of the flesh. A wink from across the room simply doesn't provoke that immediate need, and that's an important distinction. You need an action that's proportional to the response.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book flat out suggests, 'or gives a telling gaze from across the crowd.' That's just as much effort as a wink.<br /> <br /> I think at this point you're putting limits on it that the book doesn't support. Fine for your table but not something in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T09:37:33-07:00","id":569329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566508-the-three-heads-of-kerberos-clarification?p=569302#post569302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT - you know, this thing is going nowhere, so I'm just going to say we agree to disagree. From my perspective, I see people telling me what's being written in the book is wrong, and I don't see myself as in the wrong, so that's my cue to just back off here. We all play different ways, and if that's how you have fun, not my place to correct you, just as I'll be having fun with my interpretation at my game. Lets all just have fun gaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that what's written in the book is wrong, it's just that the book didn't clearly emphasize the fact that &quot;aura&quot; is an abstract OOC term, not a literal psychic halo. Fortunately, developer comments have clarified that point. But I agree, I wouldn't want to tell you how to run your game and I apologize if that's how I came off. I'm just trying to make sure the RAI is clear to others like the OP who are struggling with how to interpret the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566508-the-three-heads-of-kerberos-clarification?p=569302#post569302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The taboo / social faux pas thing was covered by the writers too. That's where its coming from. That's where I got it, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'm right there with you on this one. Obviously, since Lashing Out is a conscious and intentional action, the character must be aware that she can use her Beast to put others into fight or flight mode (even if they don't use the same terms for the phenomenon IC as we do OOC.) It follows logically that they would assume if they can do it, other vampires probably can too. And with the importance vampires place on maintaining the appearance of a civilized society, it makes sense that using that ability in polite company would be frowned upon. It's just that, as Rose said, only the user and the victim are aware of the Predatory Aura contest, which makes it very difficult to police. Much like Disciplines, I see it as a lot of &quot;nobody do this, ok!&quot; and then doing it anyway because who's going to catch you? (And then the Mekhet totally catches you because Auspex is awesome like that and drama ensues.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-26-2015, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T19:45:46-07:00","id":570814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566508-the-three-heads-of-kerberos-clarification?p=569302#post569302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The taboo / social faux pas thing was covered by the writers too. That's where its coming from. That's where I got it, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can both be taboo and subtle. It's taboo to shame someone based on the color of their skin. That's why Fox News calls them &quot;thugs&quot; and not a widely acknowledged racial slur. It doesn't mean the impact isn't there, or that they can't get away with doing it publicly. A large portion of the population thinks that's okay, so it slides. <br /> <br /> If you glare at someone, and they frenzy, people are going to look poorly upon you. There's even room for that to be flipped; some elders might fly off the handle and blame a younger vampire for lashing out, when she actually didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T22:37:31-07:00","id":572243,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that making false statements or insinuations about real people or organizations was not allowed. Maybe there are exceptions for certain people or organizations. Maybe the exception is for when certain people make the statement. Either way I find <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566508-the-three-heads-of-kerberos-clarification?p=570814#post570814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why Fox News calls them &quot;thugs&quot; and not a widely acknowledged racial slur.</div> </div> </div> </div>rude and offensive. Accusing another of using &quot;thug&quot; in place of a racial slur when the accused is referencing violent criminals makes the accuser, not the accused, guilty of equating a race with violent criminals. The premise behind the accusation is racism. There isn't a fancy name for the bigotry of the statement, but it is still bigotry, hence rude and offensive to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T23:04:20-07:00","id":572263,"title":"","content":"I don't know if you're posting from a place of earnest ignorance or partisan politics, but regardless of how you feel about Fox News, you're aware of what racial coding is, right? He's talking about that.<br /> <br /> For those who haven't heard of it, here: <a href=\"http://ideas.time.com/2012/09/06/how-to-read-political-racial-code/\" target=\"_blank\">Racial Coding</a><br /> <br /> While an article like this is speaking in reference to race, coding is a thing people do in general, and you'd probably see Kindred doing it around things pertinent to their culture, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 06-29-2015, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}